# Test: an rpc input leaf's two texts reach ze help ai --json
# VALIDATES: AC-2 of spec-both-help-texts-reach-every-surface -- an rpc entry
#            lists its input leaves, and each leaf carries `short-help` (the
#            leaf's ze:help) and `description` (the leaf's description)
# PREVENTS: extractEntryLeaves dropping the description, or the reference
#           publishing an rpc with no leaves, so an agent reads a wire method
#           and never what its parameters mean
# NOTE: this file runs ONE command on purpose, because an expect matches the
#       ACCUMULATED stdout of every command in the file. The `name` input leaf
#       of `ze-system:command-help` (internal/core/ipc/yang/ze-system-api.yang)
#       declares both texts in the tree today.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze help ai --json
expect=exit:code=0

expect=stdout:contains="wire-method": "ze-system:command-help"
expect=stdout:contains="short-help": "Command name"
expect=stdout:contains="description": "The full command name, as command-list prints it. A name in
